      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "More details: the beta adds the \"full body jitter\" fix, which in turn breaks the placement orientation of items dependent on the head's facing direction, only while using full-body, this does not affect half body.\n\nThis breaks a variety of features on avatars, and also breaks some similar systems native to VRChat, for example the recalibration clone placement is often misaligned, and you need to select \"calibrate\" a second time to make it appear in-front of you.\n\nIt is likely impossible to address both the \"full body jitter\" and the object placement behavior at the same time as one affects the other, so a toggle between the fix on/off in IK & Tracking settings would probably be the compromise to make, perhaps also surfaced as a special bool parameter to be controlled by animators/OSC so that it could be automatically turned on or off when needed by certain avatar features.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
