      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "Thanks for the responses. We'll be closing with the status that it's expected behavior now for how the root doesn't rotate while in FBT. This behavior is a necessary side effect of the greater good of solving the FBT rotation jitter issue. The expected solution for users that need the previous behavior is to use a child object of the avatar root rotationally constrained to the head yaw.",
